  "_readme": "Search terms for scripts/media_watch.py. Data, not code: edit here. Staff names are NOT listed here — they are read from our-team.html on every run, so a new hire is watched the day the team page lists them. Add people who are not on that page (a former director, a board chair) under staff_extra. outlet_feeds are read in full every run — the only way to catch a body-only mention (\"said X of Hawaii Appleseed\"), which news search does not index. `pages: N` fetches N pages of a WordPress feed (?paged=N) for an outlet whose feed holds only a few hours of stories. A feed that starts failing prints a warning. alert_feeds are Google Alerts RSS feeds ({\"name\": ..., \"url\": ...}): Google matches the phrase anywhere on the web, this script reads each page to confirm. To add one: google.com/alerts, create an alert for \"Hawaii Appleseed\" (or a staff name), set Deliver to: RSS feed, then paste the feed link here.",
